---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { business } from '../../data/business';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — Marc M"
  description="Privacy policy for marcm.fr — how your personal data is collected and used."
  lang="en"
  noindex={true}
  frPath="/politique-confidentialite"
  enPath="/en/privacy-policy"
>
  <section class="w-full bg-[var(--color-bg)] px-6 py-16 md:px-8 md:py-24">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl prose prose-neutral max-w-none">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-[var(--color-text)] mb-8">Privacy Policy</h1>

      <p class="text-[var(--color-text-muted)] mb-8">Last updated: 5 May 2026</p>

      <div class="space-y-8 text-[var(--color-text-muted)] leading-relaxed">
        <div>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-[var(--color-text)] mb-3">1. Data Controller</h2>
          <p>{business.legalName}<br />
          {business.address.street}, {business.address.zip} {business.address.city}<br />
          Email: {business.email}<br />
          Phone: {business.phone}</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-[var(--color-text)] mb-3">2. Data Collected</h2>
          <p>When you use the contact form, we collect: your name, email address, phone number (optional), and your message. This data is used solely to respond to your enquiry.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-[var(--color-text)] mb-3">3. Legal Basis</h2>
          <p>Data is processed on the basis of your consent (Article 6(1)(a) GDPR), given when you submit the contact form.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-[var(--color-text)] mb-3">4. Data Retention</h2>
          <p>Your data is retained for a maximum of 2 years from the date of last contact.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-[var(--color-text)] mb-3">5. Analytics</h2>
          <p>This site uses Umami Analytics, a privacy-friendly analytics tool that does not use cookies and does not collect personal data. No consent banner is required.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-[var(--color-text)] mb-3">6. Your Rights</h2>
          <p>Under GDPR, you have the right to access, rectify, erase, and port your personal data, as well as the right to object to processing. To exercise these rights, contact: {business.email}</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-[var(--color-text)] mb-3">7. Complaints</h2>
          <p>You have the right to lodge a complaint with the CNIL (France's data protection authority): <a href="https://www.cnil.fr" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-[var(--color-accent-text)] hover:underline">www.cnil.fr</a></p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-[var(--color-text)] mb-3">8. Data Processed on Behalf of Clients</h2>
          <p>This section applies only to clients of Marc M who have subscribed to a management or technical assistance service. It does not apply to visitors of marcm.fr.</p>

          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)] mt-5 mb-2">Access to clients' Google Business Profile accounts</h3>
          <p>As part of local marketing services, Marc M offers automated publication of posts on clients' Google Business Profile listings, generated from content already published on the client's own website (blog articles, events, offers).</p>

          <p class="mt-3">This functionality relies on the <strong>Google Business Profile API</strong> and operates under the following principles:</p>

          <ul class="list-inside list-disc space-y-2 mt-3">
            <li><strong>Explicit client authorization:</strong> each client grants access by manually adding Marc M as a <em>Manager</em> on their Google Business Profile, via the Google Business interface. No access is obtained without this explicit authorization.</li>
            <li><strong>Manual validation of every post:</strong> no post is published automatically. Each post generated by our system requires client validation in their administration panel <code class="rounded bg-[var(--color-bg-alt)] px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">/admin</code> before publication.</li>
            <li><strong>Limited OAuth scope:</strong> we request only the <code class="rounded bg-[var(--color-bg-alt)] px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">https://www.googleapis.com/auth/business.manage</code> scope, strictly necessary to read listings and publish posts. No other Google data of the client is accessed (Gmail, Drive, Calendar, Photos, etc.).</li>
            <li><strong>Secure token storage:</strong> OAuth tokens (access token, refresh token) are stored exclusively in Marc M's local macOS Keychain, encrypted at the operating system level. No token is stored in plaintext, on a remote server, or transmitted to any third party.</li>
            <li><strong>No resale, no sharing:</strong> data obtained from the Google Business Profile API (listing information, published posts, view statistics) is never resold, aggregated with other clients' data, or shared with third parties. It serves only the service for which it was collected.</li>
            <li><strong>No end-user data:</strong> we do not collect or store data of individuals consulting our clients' Google Business Profile listings (reviews left, search queries, user journeys, etc.). Such data remains within Google's perimeter.</li>
            <li><strong>Revocable control at any time:</strong> the client can revoke <em>Manager</em> access at any time via the Google Business interface (Settings → Users and permissions). This revocation immediately invalidates our ability to publish on the client's listing.</li>
          </ul>

          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)] mt-5 mb-2">Compliance with Google API Services User Data Policy</h3>
          <p>Marc M's use and transfer of information received from Google APIs adheres to the <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-[var(--color-accent-text)] hover:underline">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>, including the Limited Use requirements.</p>

          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)] mt-5 mb-2">Other Google APIs used</h3>
          <p>Marc M also uses the following Google APIs on behalf of clients, under the same principles (explicit authorization, limited scope, local secure storage, revocable):</p>
          <ul class="list-inside list-disc space-y-2 mt-3">
            <li><strong>Google Search Console API:</strong> retrieves SEO statistics for the client's site (clicks, impressions, average position, top queries) for monthly tracking reports.</li>
            <li><strong>Google Indexing API:</strong> notifies Google of new pages published on client sites to accelerate indexing.</li>
            <li><strong>Google PageSpeed Insights API:</strong> measures the technical performance of client sites.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-3">For any question regarding the processing of your data within the scope of a service, contact Marc M directly: {business.email}</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-[var(--color-text)] mb-3">9. Third-Party Services</h2>
          <p class="mb-3">This site uses only:</p>
          <ul class="list-inside list-disc space-y-2">
            <li><strong>Cloudflare Pages:</strong> website hosting (limited data processing)</li>
            <li><strong>Umami Analytics:</strong> cookie-free analytics, anonymous and aggregated data (<a href="https://umami.is/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-[var(--color-accent-text)] hover:underline">Umami privacy policy</a>)</li>
            <li><strong>Web3Forms:</strong> contact form processing (data transmitted by email only)</li>
            <li><strong>GitHub, Inc. (Microsoft):</strong> secure hosting of project files (private repository), United States, governed by the European Commission's standard contractual clauses</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-4">No Google Analytics, no Facebook Pixel, no Hotjar or equivalent.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
